    "ruleType": "detachment-rule",
    "group": "Court of the Phoenician",
    "summary": "Each of your EMPEROR'S CHILDREN units has the Sensational Performance ability: whenever such a unit is picked to fight having made a Charge move earlier in the turn, it may use the ability. If it does, for the rest of the phase it may not target any unit it was in Engagement Range of when the turn began, nor any unit already targeted this phase by an attack from another unit, and its melee weapons get +1 Strength and have their Armour Penetration improved by 1.",
